A note on HCL and MPL-2.0
-------------------------

github.com/hashicorp/hcl/v2 is under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, not MIT.
It is called out separately because it is the one dependency whose licence is
weak copyleft rather than permissive, and because it is load-bearing — HCL is
what makes TerraGraph a parser rather than a regular expression.

MPL-2.0 reciprocity is per-file: it obliges anyone who modifies HCL's own source
files to publish those modifications under MPL-2.0. TerraGraph does not modify
HCL; it imports it as a dependency. Combining an MPL-2.0 library with MIT code in
a larger work is expressly permitted (MPL-2.0 §3.3), so TerraGraph's own source
remains MIT and the distributed binaries carry both licences.

This note is a summary written for orientation, not legal advice. If your
organisation's policy restricts copyleft dependencies, the obligation attaches to
HCL and you should read MPL-2.0 yourself:
https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/


